                <pb facs="0601" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2404.</note>
                <head>[Telegram—Paraphrase—Extract.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson reports that he is in possession of evidence, given him in confidence,
                    of a plot of real magnitude to launch a counter revolution on October 15. Gen.
                    Huerta is involved, with others, and is to be recalled to-day. At present he is
                    in command of the troops sent against Zapata.mr. Wilson thinks that numerous
                    dismissals from the army and other branches of the public service will occur
                    later.</p>
            </div>
